nd a growth commit may change them under its own proof. A growth commit may not change a workflow, a hosting or deployment file, or an Astro deployment setting, or bump a package version. Every growth commit is a squash merge of one pull request (a single-parent commit whose subject ends with \" (#<number>)\"), so no commit of a growth pull request escapes the audit."},"repeatedCompile":{"bytesIdentical":true,"compiles":2}},"outcome":"pass","schema":"muxui-evidence-artifact-v1","sourceRevision":"b4bdc0dbaf20dfa5e8e60cd25f76a9d4bdcbb584","sourceTree":"5512582965032f6abc0d0200cc5841ca46a1e0ce"}